#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:7
#: 66dddf70bd284972809fb5b6e1507ce9
msgid "This section covers what you see and what you can do when in the Flight PLAN screen of Mission Planner - selected in the menu at the top of the Mission Planner application.  This section provides for planning and executing flight plans - called missions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:13
#: 3ba4e72992fa45d3bbd5cabb113c014a
msgid "The Flight PLAN Screen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:18
#: bd652018b66d4c4695b66095c42b62e8
msgid "**Upper left corner**: Displays the distance from HOME, the heading and distance from the last entered waypoint (HOME if one does not exist), and total mission trip distance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:19
#: 0492e1976f7b41639f9fcd67716404e6
msgid "**Right side**: Displays the Waypoints list for the mission. See :ref:`common-planning-a-mission-with-waypoints-and-events` for more details. Above this you can set the WPradius, Loiter Radius,and default altitude for waypoints. Altitudes can be entered in Relative (above HOME altitude),Absolute (ASL), and above Terrain. Units are set in the CONFIG/Planner page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:20
#: 5a10f4ce288547348a0c4508cca0a0cc
msgid "**Bottom** :At the bottom of the planner view you will see the latitude and longitude of the mouse cursor, its ASL (from SRTM, ie Terrain, data). You can select different map providers, Load or Save waypoints files, Read or Write the mission to the autopilot. In addition, the details of the HOME position on the map is shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/mission-planner-flight-plan.rst:22
#: c58010a9550d487dbe3e7f6081449725
msgid "Any left mouse click adds a waypoint to the mission."
msgstr ""

